@0    = ~You were in there a fair while. Are you okay? She had a bit of a predatory look about her.~
@1    = ~It's fine. She just wanted to teach me how to use my powers.~
@2    = ~It was incredible, Faren. She gave me the most amazing time.~
@3    = ~I realised she wanted to sleep with me, so I left.~
@4    = ~Yeah? Well, good for you if you got something useful out of her. Did she teach you anything good?~
@5    = ~She just wanted to sleep with me, but I left when I realised.~
@6    = ~Absolutely! She gave me the most amazing time.~
@7    = ~Huh. She was...very attractive, wasn't she? Maybe you can tell me more about it some other time...in private.~
@8    = ~You're kidding, right?~
@9    = ~Fine, <CHARNAME>. You want to go doing that kind of stuff, you can do it without stringing me along. Godsdammit! I thought you were better than that.~
@10   = ~Heh, well, I can't blame her.~
@11   = ~Don't play games, <CHARNAME>. I heard what was going on. If you want to go doing that kind of stuff, you can do it without stringing me along.~
@12   = ~Aimi's a nice girl, isn't she? I went to school with her. She was always good at mathematics, but she didn't apply herself, that's what the teacher said.~
@13   = ~Oh, she certainly applied herself last night.~
@14   = ~She is a nice girl. I enjoyed talking with her.~
@15   = ~Did you and she ever...?~
@16   = ~...that's very weird to think about, given that I remember painting the walls of the temple with her when we were six.~
@17   = ~I hope you treated her okay. She was always kind of shy.~
@18   = ~What the hell? Okay, she is pretty, but I remember painting the temple walls with her when we were six! I thought we had something good going, <CHARNAME>.~
@19   = ~I'm sorry, Faren. It was a slip, and I didn't mean to hurt you.~
@20   = ~Ha! Well, you thought wrongly.~
@21   = ~She used to natter on about the distance to the stars, I remember. Heh, it's been a long time since I saw her...~
@22   = ~Oh, gods, no. We weren't that close - she was one of the scholarly types, and I wasn't so much!~
@23   = ~Okay. Okay, fair enough. Let's get going, and we can forget about it.~
@24   = ~Classy, <CHARNAME>, really classy. Sleep with one of my old friends and then throw me off? I'm not putting up with that.~
@25   = ~The hell are you thinking, going away with that -- that--~
@26   = ~It was nothing. I was simply...practising combat.~
@27   = ~Do you really think I would put us in danger, Faren? Nothing happened.~
@28   = ~It was just a bit of fun. I don't know why you don't try it.~
@29   = ~Things got out of hand. I'm sorry if it's hurt your feelings.~
@30   = ~Seems a funny way of doing it, if you ask me.~
@31   = ~Sure. Because practising combat needs all that bumping and groaning. You smell of her, too.~
@32   = ~Just watch your back while we're in here. The Shadow Thieves are scum...even the pretty ones.~
@33   = ~You want to do that kind of stuff with Shadow Thieves, you can do it without stringing me along. I'll have no part of it.~
@34   = ~Paladin or not, that guy was a lecherous bastard. Massaging his scars, indeed - massaging his ego, more like.~
@35   = ~Still, if you're into that kind of thing, <CHARNAME>, I've got a few scars you could look at once we're alone...~
@36   = ~You think it's a good idea to get involved with that...woman, <CHARNAME>? What the hell's going on here?~
@37   = ~I... I was not myself. Bodhi used her gaze on me to control me.~
@38   = ~What's going on is that I want Bodhi, now.~
@39   = ~We need Bodhi as an ally, Faren. Don't you understand that?~
@40   = ~Yeah. I know what you mean...she's not right. Not right at all.~
@41   = ~You're kidding. Well. If you want to hook up with that bloodsucker, you can do it without me bothering you anymore.~
@42   = ~You...don't look quite right, <CHARNAME>. I don't believe you'd say that stuff if you weren't under the influence of something.~
@43   = ~It's true: I had a wonderful time, and I'd do it again!~
@44   = ~I don't know, anymore. It was all so confusing...~
@45   = ~Yeah, but you don't need to act like that with your allies. Seriously, <CHARNAME>. You'll get hurt, and not just in the emotional sense.~
@46   = ~(Faren puts his arm around your shoulders and hugs you briefly.)

Let's not talk any more about it. Come on.~
@47   = ~(Faren gives you a piercing wolf-whistle.)

Encore! Encore!~
@48   = ~Yeah, nice acting, <CHARNAME>.~
@49   = ~Wish I was the lord of a castle so I could have someone come and wash my hair. Hey, <CHARNAME>, d'you think they'd send someone to my room if I asked?~
@50   = ~Anyway, it's good to see you a bit more relaxed. You could do with it!~
@51   = ~So...what was that about? I thought we had a thing going, and then you up and leave with that weird elven guy? I had to lie there and listen to you.~
@52   = ~It was foolish, and I apologise.~
@53   = ~It's just been so difficult, Faren, with my soul gone...~
@54   = ~Then this is a good time to say that I'm not interested in you anymore.~
@55   = ~...fine. I guess everyone makes mistakes. Hells know I've made a few in my time.~
@56   = ~What the hell?!~
@57   = ~Fine. You want to take up with every guy in the area, go ahead. I don't care.~
@58   = ~<CHARNAME>, I understand why that happened. But if we have to do something like this again - I can do interrogation, I know how to do it. I've broken a man's knees in cold blood. Just - please, we can work out another way to solve things.~
@59   = ~You got something to tell me, <CHARNAME>? You and Edwin have been cosier than normal recently, as much as I hate to use the word "cosy" in relation to the guy.~
@60   = ~It was a mistake, Faren. I don't want to hurt your feelings.~
@61   = ~Nonsense. You're seeing something that isn't there.~
@62   = ~It was amazing! I never thought Edwin could be so...~
@63   = ~...okay. I see what you mean - people get funny when they're travelling together in a small group, I know that.~
@64   = ~Let's not talk about it any more, <CHARNAME>. It's kind of embarrassing, to tell the truth.~
@65   = ~Ah, okay. Imagine that guy without his robes! Gods, now I've got a bad picture in my head.~
@66   = ~...disturbing? That was the word I'd use, anyway. Heh, you go for it while you're young, that's what I say.~
@67   = ~Are you...serious? You are, aren't you?~
@68   = ~Look, I'm not going to sit by and watch you sleep with other people we're travelling with - it's not fair. I'd...rather you didn't talk to me from now on.~
@69   = ~Glad to see your taste in travelling companions has improved since you parted ways with that one.~
@70   = ~It's always good to see people from the past, though - I'm glad you got to spend some time together.~
@71   = ~You slept with him, didn't you? Godsdammit, <CHARNAME>, I wish I had a way of getting us that money so you didn't feel like you had to do this!~
@72   = ~He tricked me, Faren. I thought he'd give me information for free!~
@73   = ~There's nothing I wouldn't do to get Irenicus and help Imoen.~
@74   = ~I had no choice over this. We need his help.~
@75   = ~It wasn't entirely loathsome. I got as much enjoyment as I gave.~
@76   = ~Right.~
@77   = ~Oh, <CHARNAME> - you're so damn...~
@78   = ~If you don't mind, I'd rather not hear about it, <CHARNAME>. Let's carry on, and I'll speak to you later.~
@79   = ~You want to kill him, or shall I? I know this thing you can do to keep someone alive a very long time.~
@80   = ~I've never seen you like this before! Are you all right?~
@81   = ~No. No, I just want to move on.~
@82   = ~(Faren takes your hand and squeezes it hard.)

You're a hero, no matter what anyone might say. Let's carry on. I'll speak to you later.~
@83   = ~Fine. I'm fine. He got what he wanted out of you and then had the nerve to double-cross you. Just like every other Shadow Thief.~
@84   = ~I. Just. Look - let's not talk any more about this. I'll speak to you later, when I've calmed down.~
@85   = ~Ilona was kind of cute, wasn't she? It's nice when good things actually happen to good people.~
@86   = ~Got your fill there with your novice friend? I would've thought you'd have higher standards.~
@87   = ~What's that supposed to mean?~
@88   = ~Nothing happened, Faren. She just had a crush on me.~
@89   = ~It's all right. I just watched her sleep until the dawn.~
@90   = ~I saw the way she was ogling you. But if you want to play coy, go ahead. It's not my place to kick up a stink.~
@91   = ~And that makes it better, does it?~
@92   = ~Never mind, <CHARNAME>. Not my place to kick up a stink.~
@93   = ~What the hell was that about? Do you realise how dangerous that man is?~
@94   = ~Don't worry, Faren. Everything's under control.~
@95   = ~Nothing happened between us, if that's what you're worrying about.~
@96   = ~Oh, I do. And it's quite captivating.~
@97   = ~If you say so, <PRO_LADYLORD> Veldrin. We should head out.~
@98   = ~He's Drow, <CHARNAME>! Uh, Veldrin. Seriously. Just - watch your back, okay?~
@99   = ~<CHARNAME>, I was worried sick over where you'd gotten to!~
@100  = ~I know the Shade Lord's dead and all, but this place still gives me the creeps.~
@101  = ~It's so dangerous out here - the shadows could come and attack any moment!~
@102  = ~Just - please, watch yourself if you're going out alone.~
@103  = ~Well, that's that. Guess if you're into knights and flowery speeches, I'm not going to get anywhere.~
@104  = ~Don't look so downcast. Maybe I just wanted a quick thing?~
@105  = ~Are you jealous, Faren?~
@106  = ~Oh, I'd take you over a callow squire any day!~
@107  = ~Never change, Faren. I like you just as you are.~
@108  = ~Fair enough.~
@109  = ~No - well - maybe a bit.~
@110  = ~Heh, now that's good to hear!~
@111  = ~I polish up nice, I'll admit, but I'm never going to be like...you know, someone like him. Was just hoping you didn't have any weird expectations.~
@112  = ~You're right. I think I'd rather not get more serious with you.~
@113  = ~Okay. It would've been nice to see how things went - but I understand.~
@114  = ~That guy is...incredibly creepy. Gods know what he was getting up to with that slave of his.~
@115  = ~Can we get out of here? I'd like to see the sunshine again.~
@116  = ~Ahem...er, <CHARNAME>, you think we could give that potion of Mira's a go sometime soon? Testing the merchandise, and all that.~
@117  = ~So...you were chatting a lot with our pirate friend. Don't you think it would be better to focus on getting away from this island?~
@118  = ~Mmm, maybe. But it was a lot of fun.~
@119  = ~I've lost my soul, Faren. I think I'm entitled to a break.~
@120  = ~Nothing happened there, if that's what you're worried about.~
@121  = ~Really? What was it like? That's to say - let's just try and keep things focused. Don't want to get distracted.~
@122  = ~Are you blushing?~
@123  = ~You're right. We should head off.~
@124  = ~Look - <CHARNAME>, things are so difficult at the moment that to be perfectly honest, I'm not fussed what you do, just keep yourself safe. Okay?~
@125  = ~Of course. I'm sorry.~
@126  = ~Well. You know how it is. He's a - uh, very dashing guy.~
@127  = ~I'll have to ask whether he'd be interested in sharing.~
@128  = ~You like the idea of me and him together? That makes me uncomfortable.~
@129  = ~No - no, that'd probably be a bad idea. What with the betrayal and all.~
@130  = ~(Faren gives you a slightly strained smile, and you notice him slipping you frequent glances as you walk.)~
@131  = ~Mmmm, hello to you too, <CHARNAME>. How are you doing?~
@132  = ~What? Oh - I'm fine. Fine.~
@133  = ~I had a very disturbing dream...nice, but disturbing.~
@134  = ~Come here, Faren. I want you, right now.~
@135  = ~You're looking a bit...flustered. Want some help with that?~
@136  = ~Come here. I want you, right now.~
@137  = ~No, we should get going. Come on, let's go.~
@138  = ~Sounds better than your normal dreams. Least you got the nice part.~
@139  = ~Sounds good to me!~
@140  = ~Ah, fair enough, if you say so. Just let me get my stuff together.~
@141  = ~You and the bard make a pretty couple. Hope she's good and graceful for you - with the dancing, and all.~
@142  = ~(Looking uncharacteristically sad, Faren fiddles with a lock of his hair for a short while, avoiding your eye.)~
@143  = ~There's so much wrong with that thing with Solaufein that I can't get my head around it.~
@144  = ~Well, sometimes you have to take advantage of a situation, don't you?~
@145  = ~Faren, I did what I had to do to maintain this disguise.~
@146  = ~Nothing happened, other than spending some time with him.~
@147  = ~You mean you actually...~
@148  = ~Gods, <CHARNAME>. You're not the <PRO_MANWOMAN> I thought you were.~
@149  = ~You mean you...~
@150  = ~Gods, this place is getting to me. I wish we could get out and not have to deal with this stuff ever again.~
@151  = ~Thank the gods. This place is getting to me - I wish we could get out and not have to deal with this stuff ever again.~
@152  = ~Godsdammit, I hate this place. If we could only see the sunshine again, I'd...oh, never mind. Let's get going.~
@153  = ~So I thought you'd decided to be celibate. Not what I'd do in your situation, but...~
@154  = ~What is this new foolishness you're talking about?~
@155  = ~Course, you can always limit yourself to stuff that won't get her pregnant. It'd still be fun. You do know that, right?~
@156  = ~This conversation is over. I have no desire to discuss this matter with you, or anyone other than the lady in question.~
@157  = ~Sure thing, may the best man win. But I can't see you winning with nothing more than moping to keep her interested.~
@158  = ~Oh, come on. You've been mooning over my girlfriend for ages, now.~
@159  = ~Look, I don't want to cause trouble in the group, and I do like you - you're a nice guy. But this whole thing's making me uncomfortable. I'd appreciate it if you gave it a rest.~
